module gunbc.lambda_argument_typing_gate

import std.types { Bool, Int, List, String }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution }

// THREE LOCATED E0282 SITES WHOSE CAUSE IS UNLOCATED.
//
// This row was authored asserting a cause: that `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `emit_typed_call` binds a
// lambda argument's parameters only when the callee's BARE NAME is one of four literals, and that
// the three sites below are what that gate produces. THE SITES ARE REAL AND THE CAUSE WAS WRONG.
// The correction is made here rather than by deleting the row, because everything except the cause
// survived the refutation and is the most expensive thing in this thread to re-derive.
//
// WHAT REFUTED IT, by execution rather than by reading. A two-arm emission over the closures of
// `v2.compiler.tokenize`, `v2.compiler.parse` and `v2.lens.reference_deps`, from two separately
// built binaries whose difference was confirmed by grep before either arm ran, produced IDENTICAL
// BYTES: same file set, no differing file, no differing line, same diagnostic counts. A third arm
// deleting the binding ENTIRELY -- not generalizing it, removing it -- was also identical, which is
// what makes this conclusive rather than "the replacement happens to agree with the roster".
//
// WHY THE MECHANISM CANNOT REACH THE EMITTED BYTES, which is the durable half. The scope that gate
// computes is read for `type_env`, `module_name` and `item_registry`; its `locals` -- the field the
// lambda parameters are bound into -- has exactly ONE reader in the whole Rust emitter,
// `is_already_optional`, on the arm taken only when a node carries no resolved type. Emission runs
// off the TYPED TREE. And the declared parameter types the gate was supposed to supply are already
// consulted one stage earlier: `v1.compiler.infer` `infer_expr` passes each callee formal as the
// argument's expected type, and its `ExprLambda` arm binds the lambda's parameters from that formal
// and writes the resolved types back onto the parameter nodes. So the gate is a DEAD DECISION
// SURFACE: it reads like a live choice about lambda typing and decides nothing observable.
//
// WHAT THE SURFACE STILL IS, stated at the weaker strength the evidence supports rather than
// withdrawn outright. A four-name literal deciding a question for which the resolved declaration was
// available is a genuine bare-name-keying shape; the null refutes its CONSEQUENCE, not its shape. So
// it is a SYNTACTIC instance of that pattern with no observable consequence -- the surface decides
// nothing that reaches emitted bytes -- which is a different weight from a surface that causes
// wrongness, and it is why the literal is worth deleting as a cleanup rather than tracked as a
// defect. That cleanup carries this null as its receipt. It is not a repair of the sites below and
// must not be recorded as one.

type LambdaTypingGateSite {
  caller: DeclarationRef
  callee_spelled: String
  miss: GateMiss
}

// Why the callee misses the roster. RETAINED AS A PROPERTY OF THE SITE, NOT AS A CAUSE: the
// distinction was authored to explain how the gate declined, and the gate does not decline anything
// that reaches the emitted bytes. It survives because it is a true and cheaply checkable fact about
// each site that a later investigation may or may not find relevant -- not because it explains the
// red.
type GateMiss
  = NearMissOfARosterName { roster_name: String }
  | AbsentFromRoster

data lambda_typing_gate_sites: List<LambdaTypingGateSite> = [
  {
    caller: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.parse", decl_name: "parse_lexeme_digest"),
    callee_spelled: "fold_list",
    miss: NearMissOfARosterName { roster_name: "fold" },
  },
  {
    caller: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.std.compilers.target_model", decl_name: "target_value_expr_effect_apply_callee"),
    callee_spelled: "fold_list",
    miss: NearMissOfARosterName { roster_name: "fold" },
  },
  {
    caller: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.tokenize", decl_name: "lex_match_prefix"),
    callee_spelled: "is_prefix_of",
    miss: AbsentFromRoster,
  },
]

// THE MECHANISM VERDICT IS A TYPED ROW, NOT PROSE, because it is the fact a later reader will act
// on and the prior version of this row proves how a cause stated only in a comment gets planned
// against. The measurement is carried WITH the verdict so the refutation cannot be repeated as an
// assertion detached from what established it.
type EmittedByteDelta {
  entry_closures_measured: Int
  files_per_arm: Int
  files_differing: Int
  lines_differing: Int
}

type MechanismDisposition
  = MechanismProducesTheSites { mechanism: String }
  | MechanismRefutedByEmittedByteNull {
      mechanism: String
      delta: EmittedByteDelta
      deletion_control_also_null: Bool
    }

data lambda_typing_gate_mechanism: MechanismDisposition = MechanismRefutedByEmittedByteNull {
  mechanism: "v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_typed_call four-name collection_scope gate (map, filter, flat_map, fold)",
  delta: {
    entry_closures_measured: 3,
    files_per_arm: 258,
    files_differing: 0,
    lines_differing: 0,
  },
  deletion_control_also_null: true,
}

// WHAT NOW EXPLAINS THE THREE SITES: NOTHING. Stated as a typed disposition rather than left as an
// absence, because an unattributed red and a red attributed to a refuted mechanism are different
// states and only one of them ranks for investigation.
type SiteCauseDisposition
  = CauseAttributed { mechanism: String }
  | CauseUnlocated

data lambda_typing_gate_site_cause: SiteCauseDisposition = CauseUnlocated

// THE POPULATION IS AN UPPER BOUND, NOT A MEASUREMENT, AND THE REFUTED CAUSE DOES NOT DISTURB THAT.
//
// The three were separated from ten by intersecting the inference-failure sites with the
// arity-failure sites: a site reporting both at one position is a companion of the membership
// call-target defect and belongs to that held class, not here. That direction is sound and
// mechanical, and it never depended on why the residue fails -- only on which sites report what. The
// residue direction is the weaker one: it is defined by an ABSENCE, and holds only if arity
// reporting is complete at those positions. A suppressed downstream diagnostic would leave a
// companion looking like a member of this class.
//
// STANDING PREDICTION, which converts the bound into a measurement at no cost: when the membership
// call-target defect is repaired, all three sites below must STILL be present and still report an
// inference failure. Any that vanishes with that repair was never a member of this class.
type PopulationConfidence
  = UpperBoundPendingResidueCheck
  | MeasuredPopulation

data lambda_typing_gate_population_confidence: PopulationConfidence = UpperBoundPendingResidueCheck

// THE TRIGGER IS KEYED TO THE SITES, AND THE PREVIOUS ONE WAS THE MOST DANGEROUS LINE IN THIS ROW.
//
// It read: dies when emit_typed_call binds a lambda argument's parameters from the callee's resolved
// declaration rather than from the four-name roster. With that mechanism refuted, the trigger is
// exactly satisfiable by a change that fixes nothing -- delete the roster, retire the row, three
// sites still red. A false cause misleads a reader; a false dissolution trigger DISPOSES OF THE
// EVIDENCE, so it is the failure this correction exists to close.
//
// The replacement keys on the only fact that can honestly retire this row: the three sites emitting
// and compiling without an inference failure. No repair of any mechanism satisfies it on its own.
data lambda_typing_gate_dissolution_trigger: DissolutionCondition = unbound_dissolution(description: "dissolve-on: every site in lambda_typing_gate_sites emits and compiles with no inference-failure diagnostic at that position, established by execution against the emitted crate. NOT satisfied by any repair to v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_typed_call's bare-name gate -- that mechanism is refuted by lambda_typing_gate_mechanism and its removal is a separate cleanup with a measured zero emitted-byte delta. While lambda_typing_gate_site_cause is CauseUnlocated, no proposed repair may retire this row without the per-site green.")
